# Page templates

Choose a page template by the reader's task, not by how the page looks. This section covers **30** templates, including nested variants. Each page gives its civica adaptation, a Home Assistant boundary, two examples and acceptance checks.

| Template | Use it for |
| --- | --- |
| [Answer](answer.html) | One narrow question with the answer first. |
| [Calendar](calendar.html) | Dates and appointments with a source and time zone. |
| [Completed transaction](completed-transaction.html) | The confirmed outcome of a task. |
| [Detailed guide](detailed-guide.html) | One maintained, single-page procedure. |
| [Document collections](document-collections.html) | Related documents grouped by task. |
| [Finder](finder.html) | Search and filters over one defined collection. |
| [Case studies finder (finder)](finder/case-studies-finder.html) | Variant that searches case studies. |
| [Departments, agencies and public bodies finder (finder)](finder/departments-agencies-public-bodies-finder.html) | Variant that is a directory of organisations. |
| [Groups finder (finder)](finder/groups-finder.html) | Variant that locates groups. |
| [HMRC contacts finder (finder)](finder/hmrc-contacts-finder.html) | Variant that finds contact routes by topic. |
| [People finder (finder)](finder/people-finder.html) | Variant that lists people and roles. |
| [Search (finder)](finder/search.html) | Variant that searches indexed content across the whole site. |
| [Specialist document finder (finder)](finder/specialist-document-finder.html) | Variant that searches specialist documents. |
| [Statistical data sets finder (finder)](finder/statistical-data-sets-finder.html) | Variant that searches statistical datasets. |
| [Supergroup finder (finder)](finder/supergroup-finder.html) | Variant that groups results by broad purpose. |
| [Topical events finder (finder)](finder/topical-events-finder.html) | Variant that searches topical-event pages. |
| [World organisation finder (finder)](finder/world-organisation-finder.html) | Variant that searches worldwide organisations. |
| [Guide](guide.html) | A subject split into independent chapters. |
| [Homepage](homepage.html) | An Overview or entry page that prioritises a few routes. |
| [Mainstream browse](mainstream-browse.html) | A topic hierarchy of parent and child pages. |
| [Level one (mainstream-browse)](mainstream-browse/level-one.html) | Broad topics that lead to subtopics. |
| [Level two (mainstream-browse)](mainstream-browse/level-two.html) | Detailed destinations within a subtopic. |
| [Smart answer](smart-answer.html) | Questions that route someone to an outcome. |
| [GitHub smart answer (smart-answer)](smart-answer/github-smart-answer.html) | Version-controlled rules for complex decisions. |
| [Simple smart answer (smart-answer)](smart-answer/simple-smart-answer.html) | A short question-and-outcome tree. |
| [Special route](special-route.html) | A purpose-built page that fits no other template. |
| [Step by step nav](step-by-step-nav.html) | An ordered journey that does not track progress. |
| [Topical events](topical-events.html) | A time-bounded subject page. |
| [About page (topical-events)](topical-events/about.html) | The purpose and scope of an event collection. |
| [Transaction](transaction.html) | Context before a native flow or external service. |

## Limits and checks shared by every template

These apply to all the templates above, so the individual pages do not repeat them.

- **Reference patterns.** The templates document a local adaptation. They do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability, and civica does not install a publishing service.
- **Simulated examples.** Example dates, readings and outcomes are invented. They do not show a real device, appointment or setting changing ([WG-056](../../content/writing-guidelines/summaries.html#wg-056)).
- **No official identity.** Use the shared typography and colour roles with the household's optional identity. Official GOV.UK marks, analytics and account services are not part of the adaptation.
- **Native ownership.** Home Assistant keeps its own routes, authentication, state and permissions. A template never replaces them.

Before you rely on a template, check the examples at narrow widths, with a keyboard and without JavaScript. Test a production use against its real data and permissions before you call it supported, and report only the checks you ran ([WG-095](../../content/publish-update-retire/publish.html#wg-095)).

